          "id": "Proposition No. 1",
          "title": "Sales and Use Tax for Transportation Improvements",
          "summary": "Under Resolution 1450-0726, the sales and use tax collected in the City of Shelton for transportation would rise from two-tenths of one percent (0.2%) to three-tenths of one percent (0.3%) for ten years. The money could be used only for street and pedestrian maintenance, repair and construction projects in the city's transportation programs, or to repay debt for transportation improvements. The tax is paid by anyone making a taxable purchase in the city.",
